  "pedal": "Boss TR-2 Tremolo — focused reamp: guitar excerpts over a probe tone (mono)",
  "comment": "Short excerpts of the guitar DI dataset (captures/di/) with a steady 9 kHz sine 30 dB under the guitar's peak (the probe: a faint whistle in the headphones). The tremolo runs free, so the probe is what shows the pedal's gain at every moment, guitar or not: each setting has the probe alone (the gain's cycle, as the study measured it with a 1 kHz sine), then guitar over it — does the cycle stay the same under real playing, at -12 dB and at full level (funk: the dataset's hottest peaks), on sustained chords? One take twice (the method's floor), the lead excerpts held out of any fit. Depth 7:00: the pedal's on path without tremolo. Clock positions: 7:00 = fully counter-clockwise, 5:00 = fully clockwise; 9:00 and 3:00 pointer horizontal. Takes ordered so each step turns one or two knobs.",
